@startuml
title А4. Путь транзакции: APPROVED, DECLINED, компенсационный rollback
scale max 1600*900
autonumber
actor Client
participant Gateway as GW
participant Switch as SW
participant Authorization as AUTH
participant "BIN Lookup" as BIN
participant "Card Management" as CMS
database PostgreSQL as DB
queue RabbitMQ as MQ
participant "Transaction Logger" as LOG
== Happy path ==
Client -> GW : POST /api/transactions (0100)
GW -> GW : validate, rate limit, route
GW -> SW : HTTP sync AuthorizationRequest
SW -> SW : normalize IDs; extract BIN; resolve issuer
SW -> AUTH : POST /api/internal/authorize
AUTH -> CMS : GET /api/cards/{pan}
CMS -> DB : JPA read card
DB --> CMS : status, expiry, limits, balance
CMS --> AUTH : CardModel
AUTH -> BIN : GET /api/bin/{bin} (best-effort enrichment)
BIN --> AUTH : issuerId or empty on error
AUTH -> AUTH : check status/expiry/funds/limits
AUTH -> DB : upsert limit_usage; allocate RRN block if needed
DB --> AUTH : allowed
AUTH -> CMS : POST /api/cards/{pan}/reserve
CMS -> DB : update balance + Reservation + outbox
DB --> CMS : committed
CMS --> AUTH : reserve OK
AUTH --> SW : APPROVED + RRN + authCode
SW ->> MQ : publish TransactionRequest (async)
SW --> GW : AuthorizationResponse
GW --> Client : HTTP 200 APPROVED
MQ ->> LOG : transaction-log consumer
LOG -> DB : save transaction (eventual)
note right of SW
publisher-confirm-type=CORRELATED is configured.
LoggerClient.log currently invokes convertAndSend without explicitly
waiting on CorrelationData; verify claimed 2s confirm behavior in code.
end note
== Declined: BLOCKED card ==
Client -> GW : POST /api/transactions (0100)
GW -> SW : HTTP sync
SW -> AUTH : POST authorize
AUTH -> CMS : GET card
CMS --> AUTH : CardModel(status=BLOCKED)
AUTH -> AUTH : DeclineOutcome.CARD_BLOCKED
AUTH --> SW : DECLINED + reason
SW ->> MQ : publish declined transaction (async)
SW --> GW : DECLINED
GW --> Client : HTTP 200 + responseCode/reason
MQ ->> LOG : asynchronous persistence
note over AUTH,CMS
Status rejection occurs before limit update and reserve.
Source: AuthServiceImpl.authorize(), DeclineOutcome.java.
end note
== Reversal / rollback if logger publish fails ==
Client -> GW : POST transaction (0100)
GW -> SW : HTTP sync
SW -> AUTH : authorize
AUTH -> CMS : GET card, then POST reserve
CMS -> DB : reduce balance; persist Reservation
DB --> CMS : committed
CMS --> AUTH : reserve OK
AUTH --> SW : APPROVED + RRN
SW ->> MQ : publish log message
MQ --> SW : no ack / publish exception (failure path)
SW -> AUTH : POST /api/internal/rollback (rrn, pan, amount)
AUTH -> CMS : POST /api/cards/{pan}/rollback
CMS -> DB : restore balance; Reservation → ROLLED_BACK
DB --> CMS : committed
CMS --> AUTH : rollback response
AUTH --> SW : rollback APPROVED or DECLINED
SW --> GW : system error / responseCode 96 per stated contract
GW --> Client : DECLINED / system error
note over SW,AUTH
RouteService performs the compensation using rollback endpoint.
The request is not necessarily a new ISO mti=0400 message;
AuthorizationRequest exposes a reversal factory, but verify caller path.
Source: RouteService.java, AuthorizationClient.java, AuthorizationRequest.java.
end note
@enduml
